379 Can. 9 . "On the help of God. Divine gift is that we think rightly and that
let us restrain our feet from falsehood and injustice; because how many times we do well,
God, so that we may work, works in us and with us.”

897 (7) The kiss of a woman, as nature does not incline to it, is a mortal sin;
On the other hand, the carnal act, however nature inclines to it, is not a sin, especially
if he who exercises it is tempted.

1340 He also anathematizes Manichaeus with his henchmen, who with their dreams that the Son of
God had not assumed a true body, but a fantastic one, they completely destroyed the truth

of humanity in Christ;
